workedExamples.question_text:
An inquiry surveys $24$ households about their preferred way to receive community notices. Its hypothesis is “More than half of households prefer email.”

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=3mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,16);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.2,0);
\foreach \y in {0,4,8,12,16} {\draw[black] (-0.08,\y)--(0,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.08,\y) {$\y$};}
\draw[black] (0.5,0) rectangle (1.2,14);
\draw[black] (1.7,0) rectangle (2.4,6);
\draw[black] (2.9,0) rectangle (3.6,4);
\node[above] at (0.85,14) {$14$};
\node[above] at (2.05,6) {$6$};
\node[above] at (3.25,4) {$4$};
\node[below] at (0.85,0) {Email};
\node[below] at (2.05,0) {Print};
\node[below] at (3.25,0) {App};
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.65,8) {Households};
\node at (2.05,19) {Preferred notice method};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Does the sample data support the hypothesis? Explain using the figures. State a limitation if all surveyed households came from one apartment building.

